# Android auto-install

When you finish a turn that changed code shipping in the Capacitor Android app, **install to the connected phone before ending** — do not wait for the user to ask.

## What counts as shipping code

- `app/**`, `src/**`, `index.html`, `public/**` (if used by the web bundle)
- Capacitor / Android native config that affects the build
- `.env` values baked into Vite (`VITE_*`) when they must land in the APK

Skip install for docs-only, store-assets QA dumps, or pure investigation with no file edits.

## How to install

```powershell
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/install-android-device.ps1
```

Or: `npm run mobile:install`

Use Shell with full permissions (`all`). Budget several minutes (`block_until_ms` ≥ 600000).

## Failure handling

- If `INSTALL_FAILED_UPDATE_INCOMPATIBLE`, uninstall `com.esnaftaucuz.app` then reinstall (the script already retries this).
- If no device: report clearly; do not pretend install succeeded.
- Tell the user briefly that the phone was updated (or why it was skipped).
